# No spare or redundant solutions

Ship only what is needed for the current request. Do not leave unused alternatives "just in case".

- Do not add unused CSS classes, modifiers, flags, or config
- Do not implement several variants when one solution is enough
- Do not introduce abstractions, wrappers, or naming schemes that are not used yet
- If the user asks for options, show them in chat and apply only the chosen one

```css
/* BAD: spare modifier that is never used in HTML */
.footer-course--cream {
  background: #f4ead7;
}

/* GOOD: the one style that is actually applied */
.footer-course {
  background: #fff;
}
```
